#!/bin/sh
set -e

cat <<'EOF'

pkcs11-proxy-ng-daemon installed.

NEXT STEPS:
1. Edit /etc/pkcs11-proxy-ng/proxy.toml and replace the
   [backend].module placeholder with a real PKCS#11 .so path
   (e.g. /usr/lib/softhsm/libsofthsm2.so).
2. Start the service:
       rc-service pkcs11-proxy-ng start
3. Enable on boot (after you've verified step 2 works):
       rc-update add pkcs11-proxy-ng default

The default config listens on 0.0.0.0:7512 with auth="none". This is
intended for deployments behind external network protection
(Kubernetes NetworkPolicy, VPC private subnet, sidecar/mesh policy).
The daemon emits a loud WARN at startup so the choice is visible in
operator log scans. Switch to mTLS via the commented template in
/etc/pkcs11-proxy-ng/proxy.toml if you cannot guarantee the network
boundary.
EOF

exit 0
